this"],[14.713,0.362,"world"],[15.088,0.1,"of"],[15.2,0.487,"change"],[15.7,0.1,"and"],[15.812,0.575,"suffering"]]},{"layout":"steps","headline":"The great cycle","visual":["Brahma's day begins","All beings emerge","Brahma's night falls","All dissolve","Day returns"],"L":["L4"],"say":"Lesson four. Everything in creation is cyclic. Creation and dissolution follow each other in vast cosmic cycles. All beings emerge at the dawn of Brahma's day and dissolve at its night, then emerge again. Only God's own abode stands outside the turning wheel.","start":222.696,"at":223.272,"end":241.968,"words":[[0.062,0.325,"Lesson"],[0.4,0.438,"four"],[1.238,0.463,"Everything"],[1.712,0.163,"in"],[1.887,0.575,"creation"],[2.475,0.15,"is"],[2.638,0.725,"cyclic"],[3.763,0.662,"Creation"],[4.438,0.138,"and"],[4.588,0.7,"dissolution"],[5.3,0.412,"follow"],[5.725,0.2,"each"],[5.938,0.312,"other"],[6.263,0.188,"in"],[6.463,0.4,"vast"],[6.875,0.412,"cosmic"],[7.3,0.625,"cycles"],[8.325,0.225,"All"],[8.562,0.312,"beings"],[8.887,0.537,"emerge"],[9.45,0.125,"at"],[9.588,0.1,"the"],[9.7,0.312,"dawn"],[10.025,0.125,"of"],[10.162,0.388,"Brahma's"],[10.562,0.35,"day"],[10.925,0.125,"and"],[11.062,0.487,"dissolve"],[11.562,0.087,"at"],[11.662,0.163,"its"],[11.838,0.4,"night"],[12.75,0.237,"then"],[13.0,0.4,"emerge"],[13.412,0.438,"again"],[14.25,0.237,"Only"],[14.5,0.375,"God's"],[14.887,0.225,"own"],[15.125,0.388,"abode"],[15.525,0.487,"stands"],[16.025,0.537,"outside"],[16.575,0.075,"the"],[16.663,0.375,"turning"],[17.05,0.4,"wheel"]]},{"layout":"compare","headline":"Two paths after death","visual":["The path of light | The path of darkness","Self-knowledge | Ignorance","Leads to liberation | Leads to heaven, then rebirth","No return | Return"],"L":["L5"],"say":"Lesson five. There are two paths after death, light and darkness. The path of light, the path of self-knowledge, leads to liberation, with no return. The path of darkness, the path of ignorance, may lead to heaven for a while, but then back to rebirth. The yogi who knows this is never confused.","start":241.968,"at":242.544,"end":263.112,"words":[[0.062,0.325,"Lesson"],[0.4,0.512,"five"],[1.288,0.113,"There"],[1.413,0.1,"are"],[1.525,0.225,"two"],[1.762,0.463,"paths"],[2.237,0.312,"after"],[2.562,0.487,"death"],[3.413,0.388,"light"],[3.812,0.125,"and"],[3.95,0.662,"darkness"],[5.0,0.075,"The"],[5.088,0.325,"path"],[5.425,0.138,"of"],[5.575,0.388,"light"],[5.987,0.125,"the"],[6.125,0.338,"path"],[6.475,0.087,"of"],[6.575,0.875,"self-knowledge"],[7.787,0.375,"leads"],[8.175,0.113,"to"],[8.3,0.688,"liberation"],[9.012,0.175,"with"],[9.2,0.212,"no"],[9.425,0.55,"return"],[10.363,0.075,"The"],[10.45,0.312,"path"],[10.775,0.113,"of"],[10.9,0.588,"darkness"],[11.512,0.113,"the"],[11.637,0.312,"path"],[11.963,0.1,"of"],[12.075,0.625,"ignorance"],[12.925,0.225,"may"],[13.162,0.237,"lead"],[13.412,0.087,"to"],[13.512,0.338,"heaven"],[13.863,0.15,"for"],[14.025,0.075,"a"],[14.113,0.475,"while"],[14.95,0.2,"but"],[15.162,0.188,"then"],[15.363,0.237,"back"],[15.613,0.113,"to"],[15.738,0.625,"rebirth"],[16.75,0.062,"The"],[16.825,0.463,"yogi"],[17.3,0.175,"who"],[17.488,0.362,"knows"],[17.863,0.212,"this"],[18.087,0.15,"is"],[18.25,0.312,"never"],[18.575,0.762,"confused"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Spiritual Practice Surpasses All Ritual Merit","visual":["Study, sacrifice, austerity, charity","All bring merit","The steady yogi goes beyond them all"],"L":["L6"],"say":"Lesson six. Spiritual practice surpasses all ritual merit. Whatever good comes from studying the Vedas, from sacrifices, austerities and charity, the yogi who knows these truths goes beyond all of it, and reaches the supreme, eternal abode. Inner union outweighs outer religion.","start":263.112,"at":263.688,"end":283.656,"words":[[0.075,0.312,"Lesson"],[0.4,0.512,"six"],[1.275,0.562,"Spiritual"],[1.85,0.562,"practice"],[2.425,0.688,"surpasses"],[3.125,0.3,"all"],[3.438,0.362,"ritual"],[3.812,0.475,"merit"],[4.688,0.325,"Whatever"],[5.025,0.237,